# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this, every `docker build` uploads the whole repo -- including `.venv`,
# which on this machine is over a gigabyte of Windows binaries -- and then throws
# most of it away. It also makes the build context include the local database files
# and generated reports, so an image's contents change depending on what happens to
# be in the working directory.

# Virtual environments. `.venv` is a Windows build here and a Linux one in the
# image; copying it in is at best dead weight and at worst a shadowing hazard, since
# `/app/.venv` would be found before the installed `/opt/venv`.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Version control and CI. `.git` in particular is large and never needed: the build
# copies named directories, not the repository.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Local data. `data/runtime/` holds SQLite files, load-test output and reconciliation
# JSON from previous runs, and must never be copied into an image.
#
# `data/*` and `!data/model` rather than `data/` and `!data/model`: .dockerignore
# cannot re-include a file whose *parent* directory is excluded, so excluding `data/`
# and then re-adding the subdirectory silently does nothing -- the build fails with
# `COPY data/model: not found`, which reads like a missing file rather than like a
# negation that never applied. `data/model/` is a runtime input and is copied
# explicitly by the Dockerfile.
data/*
!data/model
data/runtime/

# Generated reports and caches. Reproduced by `make evidence` on demand, and stale
# copies in an image are worse than none: a report that contradicts the code it
# shipped with is a claim nobody can check.
docs/
!docs/
data/runtime/reports/

# Python build and cache artefacts. Present in a working tree after running the
# suite locally, and large.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml

# Generated gRPC stubs are committed on purpose (see CLAUDE.md: nothing warns you if
# they go stale), so they are deliberately NOT excluded.

# Local environment and editor files.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
